# The other arity of the SAME C symbol, in its own module.
#
# `printf` again, `<stdio.h>` again, a different value type. Two `extern`
# groups in two modules naming one symbol is not a collision: the probes
# are mangled per module (panel 053), and the call goes through the
# header's own prototype, so C sees one function and Heroes sees two
# bindings. `format` says `lent` (panel 171): `printf` reads it while it runs
# and keeps nothing. `value` stands past `printf`'s `...`, where C reads what
# it is handed as whatever type it asks for, so a read-only lend there is
# refused (panel 217's R3(c), defect 2102, 2026-10-17) and it takes a lease, a
# copy C may write; `twoarity-lent/` is the same program with the lend, refused.

extern "stdio.h"
    function printf(format: cstr lent, value: cstr) -> i32

# The wrapper takes two `str`, lends the format inside itself, as `as_int.hero`
# says why, and hands the value over as a lease it ends once `printf` returns.
function say(format: str, value: str) -> i32
    copy: cstr @= value.lease()
    said = printf(format: format.cstr(), value: copy)
    end_lease(@copy)
    return said
